nb_v4.py: NOR-BWIM v4 re-analysis. Runs used: d1A: R1, R2, R3, R4, R7, R8, R9; d2A: R15, R16, R17, R18, R11, R12, R13, R14; d2B: R15r, R16r, R17r, R18r, R11r, R12r, R13r, R14r; multi: M1, M2

==============================================================================
TASK 1. Per-channel constant C = int(eps dx)/GVW (microstrain*m/t)
Day-1 GVW: driver-reported per pass (Moghadam 2022 dissertation, hdl:10919/111390, Table 2.4); day-2 GVW: static weigh-station weights (same source, Table 2.1, Sec. 2.2.3). Day-1 runs R1-R4 = Truck 1, R7-R9 = Truck 2 (both 3-axle); day-2 lane A R11-R14 = Truck 3 (3-axle), R15-R18 = Truck 4 (5-axle).
Ratio CIs: Welch t on log|C| (empirical scatter, small n). TOST = 90% CI inside [1-m, 1+m]. chi2_p uses the noise sd from vehicle-free windows (nb_tests).

