TASK 4. Estimators, out-of-sample. C_j = mean(Ix_j/GVW) over calibration runs only; Sigma = covariance of vehicle-free integrals for the test run's window length (from quiet data, so it never contains the test run), scaled by v_test^2. Schemes: LOO = leave-one-run-out; LOTO = calibrate on one truck, test on the other; IN = in-sample (C from all runs incl. the test run) for comparison.

Diagnostic: scatter of crossing residuals (I_j - C_j W, all runs) versus the vehicle-free noise covariance at each run's window and speed
